{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-04-17","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-04-17","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-04-17","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2939","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"D000230","fullName":"Rep. Davis, Donald G. [D-NC-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"T000463","fullName":"Rep. Turner, Michael R. [R-OH-10]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"M001218","fullName":"Rep. McCormick, Richard [R-GA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"H001098","fullName":"Rep. Hamadeh, Abraham J. [R-AZ-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"},{"bioguideId":"B001324","fullName":"Rep. Bell, Wesley [D-MO-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"L000598","fullName":"Rep. LaLota, Nick [R-NY-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"C001123","fullName":"Rep. Cisneros, Gilbert Ray [D-CA-31]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"W000804","fullName":"Rep. Wittman, Robert J. [R-VA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-11","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"B001298","fullName":"Rep. Bacon, Don [R-NE-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"V000138","fullName":"Rep. Vindman, Eugene Simon [D-VA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-08-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"L000597","fullName":"Rep. Lee, Laurel M. [R-FL-15]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"M001230","fullName":"Rep. Mackenzie, Ryan [R-PA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"M001241","fullName":"Rep. Min, Dave [D-CA-47]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-18","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T21:01:59+00:00","id":"hr2939-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-17","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-17","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"2939","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"K000399","district":2,"fullName":"Rep. Kiggans, Jennifer A. [R-VA-2]","party":"R","state":"VA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-17","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Drone Espionage Act</strong></p><p>This bill makes it a federal crime under the Espionage Act to engage in certain activities related to obtaining, receiving, or transmitting video of national defense information. The term <em>national defense information</em> means information or other material that is related to national defense.</p><p>The Espionage Act prohibits certain activities related to obtaining, receiving, or transmitting national defense information that could harm the United States or aid a foreign nation. Under current law, the prohibitions only apply if national defense information is obtained, received, or transmitted by certain means,&nbsp;such as a sketch, photograph, photographic negative, blueprint, plan, map, model, instrument, appliance, document, writing, or note. Under current law,&nbsp;a violator is subject to criminal penalties—a fine, a prison term of up to 10 years, or both.</p><p>This bill makes the criminal prohibitions under the Espionage Act applicable if national defense information is obtained, received, or transmitted by means of video. Under this bill, a violator is subject to the same penalties as under existing law—a fine, a prison term of up to 10 years, or both.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-22T16:39:49Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Drone Espionage Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-22T16:40:14Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-22T16:40:14Z"}
